TERMS_18 = [
    ("shellcode", "Shellcode", ["shell code", "shellcodes", "code d'exploitation", "msimbo wa shell"], "attacks", "binary code on a screen", {"fr": "Shellcode", "sw": "Shellcode", "rw": "Shellcode"},
     "A small piece of machine code that an attacker makes a vulnerable program run after exploiting a flaw, often to open a remote command shell or download more malware.",
     "Defenders stop it with patches, memory protections (DEP, ASLR), endpoint security that spots unusual behaviour, and by not running untrusted files or macros.",
     "Un petit morceau de code machine qu'un attaquant fait exécuter à un programme vulnérable après avoir exploité une faille, souvent pour ouvrir un shell à distance ou télécharger d'autres malwares.",
     "Les défenseurs l'arrêtent avec des correctifs, des protections mémoire (DEP, ASLR), des solutions de sécurité qui repèrent les comportements anormaux, et en n'exécutant pas de fichiers ou macros non fiables.",
     "Agace gato ka code ya mashini umushimusi atuma porogaramu ifite intege nke ikora nyuma yo gukoresha ikosa, akenshi kugira ngo afungure shell ya kure cyangwa akurure izindi malware.",
     "Abarinzi barabuza hakoreshejwe patches, uburinzi bwa memory (DEP, ASLR), ibikoresho bya endpoint bibona imikorere idasanzwe, no kudakoresha dosiye cyangwa macros zitizewe.",
     "Kipande kidogo cha msimbo wa mashine ambacho mshambulizi hufanya programu yenye udhaifu iendeshe baada ya kutumia hitilafu, mara nyingi kufungua shell ya mbali au kupakua programu hasidi zaidi.",
     "Watetezi huizuia kwa viraka, ulinzi wa kumbukumbu (DEP, ASLR), usalama wa endpoint unaogundua tabia isiyo ya kawaida, na kutoendesha faili au macros zisizoaminika."),
    ("exploit-chain", "Exploit chain", ["exploit chains", "chained exploits", "vulnerability chaining", "chaîne d'exploits", "chaine d'exploits", "mnyororo wa exploit"], "attacks", "chain of linked blocks", {"fr": "Chaîne d'exploits", "sw": "Mnyororo wa exploits", "rw": "Urunana rw'exploits"},
     "Several vulnerabilities used one after another to reach a goal that no single flaw would allow, for example a web flaw to get in, then a second flaw to gain full administrator control.",
     "Fixing even one link breaks the chain, which is why patching all known flaws and limiting privileges matters. Layered defences (defence in depth) make chains harder to build.",
     "Plusieurs vulnérabilités utilisées l'une après l'autre pour atteindre un objectif qu'aucune faille seule ne permettrait, par exemple une faille web pour entrer, puis une seconde pour obtenir le contrôle administrateur complet.",
     "Corriger ne serait-ce qu'un maillon casse la chaîne, d'où l'importance de corriger toutes les failles connues et de limiter les privilèges. Les défenses en couches rendent les chaînes plus difficiles à construire.",
     "Intege nke nyinshi zikoreshwa imwe nyuma y'indi kugira ngo hagerweho intego nta ntege nke imwe yonyine yemerera, urugero ikosa rya web ryo kwinjira, hanyuma irya kabiri ryo kubona ubuyobozi bwuzuye.",
     "Gukosora n'akaziga kamwe bica urunana, ni yo mpamvu gukosora intege nke zose zizwi no kugabanya uburenganzira ari ingenzi. Uburinzi mu byiciro bituma urunana rugorana kubaka.",
     "Udhaifu kadhaa unaotumika mmoja baada ya mwingine kufikia lengo ambalo hakuna hitilafu moja ingeruhusu, mfano hitilafu ya wavuti kuingia, kisha ya pili kupata udhibiti kamili wa msimamizi.",
     "Kurekebisha hata kiungo kimoja huvunja mnyororo, ndiyo maana kusasisha udhaifu wote unaojulikana na kupunguza haki ni muhimu. Ulinzi wa tabaka hufanya minyororo kuwa ngumu kujenga."),
    ("zombie-device", "Zombie computer", ["zombie computer", "zombie device", "zombie", "zombie pc", "ordinateur zombie", "kompyuta zombie", "mashine zombie"], "malware", "infected computers network", {"fr": "Ordinateur zombie", "sw": "Kompyuta zombie", "rw": "Mudasobwa zombie"},
     "A computer, phone or smart device secretly taken over by malware and controlled remotely, usually as part of a botnet, without its owner knowing.",
     "Signs include a slow device, high data use and strange network activity. Zombies are used for spam and DDoS attacks. Keep devices updated, change default passwords on routers and cameras, and run security scans.",
     "Un ordinateur, téléphone ou objet connecté pris en secret par un malware et contrôlé à distance, généralement dans un botnet, à l'insu de son propriétaire.",
     "Signes : appareil lent, forte consommation de données, activité réseau étrange. Les zombies servent au spam et aux attaques DDoS. Mettez à jour vos appareils, changez les mots de passe par défaut des routeurs et caméras, et lancez des analyses.",
     "Mudasobwa, telefone cyangwa igikoresho cy'ubwenge cyigaruriwe rwihishwa na malware kigategekwa kure, akenshi muri botnet, nyirayo atabizi.",
     "Ibimenyetso: igikoresho gitinda, gukoresha amakuru menshi n'ibikorwa bidasanzwe kuri network. Zombies zikoreshwa muri spam no mu bitero bya DDoS. Vugurura ibikoresho, uhindure amagambo y'ibanga asanzwe ya router na kamera, ukore scan.",
     "Kompyuta, simu au kifaa mahiri kilichotekwa kwa siri na programu hasidi na kudhibitiwa kwa mbali, kwa kawaida kama sehemu ya botnet, bila mmiliki kujua.",
     "Dalili ni kifaa cha polepole, matumizi makubwa ya data na shughuli za ajabu za mtandao. Zombie hutumika kwa spam na mashambulizi ya DDoS. Sasisha vifaa, badilisha nywila chaguo-msingi za router na kamera, na ufanye skani."),
    ("eavesdropping-wiretapping", "Eavesdropping and wiretapping", ["eavesdropping", "wiretapping", "wire tapping", "network eavesdropping", "passive attack", "écoute clandestine", "ecoute clandestine", "interception", "kusikiliza kwa siri", "kunasa mawasiliano"], "attacks", "headphones and network cable", {"fr": "Écoute clandestine et interception", "sw": "Kusikiliza kwa siri na kunasa mawasiliano", "rw": "Gutega amatwi no gufata itumanaho"},
     "Secretly listening to or capturing communications such as calls, messages or network traffic without permission. A passive attack only watches; it does not change the data.",
     "Public Wi-Fi, unencrypted websites and unprotected links make it easier. Use HTTPS, a trusted VPN on public networks, and end-to-end encrypted messaging; avoid sharing sensitive information over plain SMS or open Wi-Fi.",
     "Écouter ou capturer en secret des communications (appels, messages, trafic réseau) sans autorisation. Une attaque passive ne fait qu'observer sans modifier les données.",
     "Wi-Fi public, sites non chiffrés et liaisons non protégées la facilitent. Utilisez HTTPS, un VPN de confiance sur les réseaux publics et une messagerie chiffrée de bout en bout ; évitez les infos sensibles par SMS simple ou Wi-Fi ouvert.",
     "Gutega amatwi cyangwa gufata itumanaho nko guhamagara, ubutumwa cyangwa amakuru ya network rwihishwa nta ruhushya. Igitero cya passive kireba gusa, ntigihindura amakuru.",
     "Wi-Fi rusange, imbuga zidafunze n'imiyoboro idakingiye biraryorohereza. Koresha HTTPS, VPN wizeye ku miyoboro rusange n'ubutumwa bufunze impande zombi; irinde gusangiza amakuru y'ibanga kuri SMS isanzwe cyangwa Wi-Fi ifunguye.",
     "Kusikiliza au kunasa mawasiliano kama simu, ujumbe au trafiki ya mtandao kwa siri bila ruhusa. Shambulio tulivu hutazama tu, halibadilishi data.",
     "Wi-Fi ya umma, tovuti zisizosimbwa na viungo visivyolindwa hurahisisha. Tumia HTTPS, VPN inayoaminika kwenye mitandao ya umma na ujumbe uliosimbwa mwanzo hadi mwisho; epuka kushiriki taarifa nyeti kwa SMS ya kawaida au Wi-Fi wazi."),
    ("domain-dns-hijacking", "Domain hijacking and DNS hijacking", ["domain hijacking", "dns hijacking", "domain theft", "registrar hijacking", "détournement de domaine", "detournement de domaine", "détournement dns", "kutekwa kwa kikoa"], "attacks", "website address being redirected", {"fr": "Détournement de domaine et DNS", "sw": "Kutekwa kwa kikoa na DNS", "rw": "Kwiba domain no guhindura DNS"},
     "Domain hijacking is taking control of a website's domain name, usually through its registrar account. DNS hijacking changes where a name points (on a router, a resolver or the domain's records) so visitors reach a fake server.",
     "Victims see the real address but land on a criminal's copy, used for phishing or malware. Protect registrar accounts with MFA and registry lock, secure routers (change default passwords), and use DNSSEC and trusted DNS.",
     "Le détournement de domaine consiste à prendre le contrôle du nom de domaine d'un site, généralement via le compte chez le registrar. Le détournement DNS change la destination d'un nom (routeur, résolveur ou enregistrements) pour que les visiteurs atteignent un faux serveur.",
     "Les victimes voient la vraie adresse mais arrivent sur une copie criminelle, utilisée pour l'hameçonnage ou les malwares. Protégez les comptes registrar par MFA et verrouillage, sécurisez les routeurs (changez les mots de passe par défaut), utilisez DNSSEC et un DNS de confiance.",
     "Kwiba domain ni ugufata ubuyobozi bw'izina ry'urubuga, akenshi unyuze kuri konti y'ikigo kiyandikisha. Guhindura DNS bihindura aho izina rigana (kuri router, resolver cyangwa inyandiko za domain) bityo abasura bakagera kuri seriveri y'impimbano.",
     "Abagizweho ingaruka babona aderesi nyayo ariko bagera kuri kopi y'umugizi wa nabi, ikoreshwa muri phishing cyangwa malware. Rinda konti za registrar ukoresheje MFA na registry lock, rinda router (hindura amagambo y'ibanga asanzwe), koresha DNSSEC na DNS yizewe.",
     "Kutekwa kwa kikoa ni kuchukua udhibiti wa jina la kikoa cha tovuti, kwa kawaida kupitia akaunti ya msajili. Kutekwa kwa DNS hubadilisha jina linakoelekea (kwenye router, resolver au rekodi za kikoa) ili wageni wafike kwenye seva bandia.",
     "Waathirika huona anwani halisi lakini hufika kwenye nakala ya mhalifu, inayotumika kwa hadaa au programu hasidi. Linda akaunti za msajili kwa MFA na registry lock, linda router (badilisha nywila chaguo-msingi), tumia DNSSEC na DNS inayoaminika."),
    ("zip-fork-bomb", "Zip bomb and fork bomb", ["zip bomb", "decompression bomb", "fork bomb", "bombe zip", "bombe de décompression", "bombe de decompression", "bombe fork", "bomu la zip"], "attacks", "compressed file exploding", {"fr": "Bombe zip et bombe fork", "sw": "Zip bomb na fork bomb", "rw": "Zip bomb na fork bomb"},
     "Resource-exhaustion tricks: a zip bomb is a tiny archive that expands to a huge size and overwhelms a scanner or disk, and a fork bomb is a program that keeps creating copies of itself until a system freezes.",
     "They cause denial of service rather than data theft. Defences include limits on file expansion size and depth, process and memory limits (quotas), and scanning attachments in a sandbox rather than directly on production servers.",
     "Astuces d'épuisement de ressources : une bombe zip est une petite archive qui s'étend en une taille énorme et sature un scanner ou un disque ; une bombe fork est un programme qui se recopie sans cesse jusqu'à figer un système.",
     "Elles causent un déni de service plutôt qu'un vol de données. Défenses : limites de taille et de profondeur de décompression, quotas de processus et de mémoire, et analyse des pièces jointes dans un bac à sable plutôt que sur les serveurs de production.",
     "Amayeri yo gusimbura ibikoresho: zip bomb ni dosiye ntoya ifunguka ikaba nini cyane ikananiza scanner cyangwa disiki, naho fork bomb ni porogaramu yikoporora kugeza sisitemu ihagaze.",
     "Bitera kubuza serivisi aho kwiba amakuru. Uburinzi: imipaka y'ubunini n'ubujyakuzimu bwo gufungura, imipaka ya process na memory, no gusuzuma attachments muri sandbox aho kuba ku maseriveri y'ibikorwa.",
     "Mbinu za kumaliza rasilimali: zip bomb ni faili ndogo inayopanuka kuwa kubwa sana na kuzidi kichanganuzi au diski, na fork bomb ni programu inayojinakili hadi mfumo ugandishwe.",
     "Husababisha kunyimwa huduma badala ya wizi wa data. Ulinzi: mipaka ya ukubwa na kina cha upanuzi, kikomo cha michakato na kumbukumbu, na kuchanganua viambatisho kwenye sandbox badala ya seva za uzalishaji."),
    ("legacy-network-attacks", "Ping of death and teardrop", ["ping of death", "teardrop attack", "land attack", "smurf and ping of death", "ping de la mort", "attaque teardrop", "ping ya kifo"], "attacks", "network cable and warning sign", {"fr": "Ping de la mort et teardrop", "sw": "Ping of death na teardrop", "rw": "Ping of death na teardrop"},
     "Old denial-of-service attacks that crashed systems by sending malformed or oversized network packets. They worked on unpatched operating systems from the 1990s.",
     "Modern systems are patched against them, but they teach a lasting lesson: software must validate network input and be kept updated. Firewalls and up-to-date operating systems block these old tricks.",
     "Anciennes attaques par déni de service qui faisaient planter les systèmes en envoyant des paquets réseau malformés ou trop gros. Elles fonctionnaient sur des systèmes non corrigés des années 1990.",
     "Les systèmes modernes sont corrigés, mais la leçon demeure : le logiciel doit valider les entrées réseau et rester à jour. Pare-feu et systèmes à jour bloquent ces vieilles ruses.",
     "Ibitero bya kera byo kubuza serivisi byasenyaga sisitemu byohereza ibipaki bya network bitameze neza cyangwa binini cyane. Byakoraga ku bikoresho bidavuguruye byo mu myaka ya 1990.",
     "Sisitemu zigezweho zarakosowe, ariko isomo rirahari: porogaramu igomba kugenzura ibyinjira muri network kandi ikavugururwa. Firewall na sisitemu zivuguruye bibuza ayo mayeri ya kera.",
     "Mashambulizi ya zamani ya kunyima huduma yaliyoangusha mifumo kwa kutuma pakiti za mtandao zenye kasoro au kubwa kupita kiasi. Yalifanya kazi kwenye mifumo ya miaka ya 1990 isiyosasishwa.",
     "Mifumo ya kisasa imesasishwa dhidi yake, lakini somo linabaki: programu lazima ithibitishe ingizo la mtandao na isasishwe. Firewall na mifumo iliyosasishwa huzuia hila hizo za zamani."),
    ("ntp-memcached-amplification", "NTP and Memcached amplification", ["ntp amplification", "memcached amplification", "dns amplification", "reflection amplification", "amplification ddos", "amplification ntp", "amplification memcached", "amplificación"], "attacks", "small request large flood", {"fr": "Amplification NTP et Memcached", "sw": "Amplification ya NTP na Memcached", "rw": "Amplification ya NTP na Memcached"},
     "DDoS tricks where an attacker sends small requests with a forged victim address to misconfigured public servers (NTP, DNS, Memcached) that answer with much larger replies aimed at the victim.",
     "The 2018 Memcached attacks reached record sizes this way. Operators should not leave such services open to the whole internet and should filter spoofed traffic; victims use DDoS protection and rate limiting.",
     "Astuces DDoS où un attaquant envoie de petites requêtes avec l'adresse falsifiée de la victime à des serveurs publics mal configurés (NTP, DNS, Memcached) qui répondent par des réponses bien plus grosses dirigées vers la victime.",
     "Les attaques Memcached de 2018 ont atteint des volumes records ainsi. Les exploitants ne doivent pas laisser ces services ouverts à tout Internet et doivent filtrer le trafic usurpé ; les victimes utilisent une protection DDoS et la limitation de débit.",
     "Amayeri ya DDoS aho umushimusi yohereza ibyifuzo bito afite aderesi y'uwahohotewe y'impimbano kuri seriveri rusange zitashyizweho neza (NTP, DNS, Memcached) zisubiza ibisubizo binini cyane byerekeza ku wahohotewe.",
     "Ibitero bya Memcached byo mu 2018 byageze ku bunini butigeze bubaho bityo. Abayobora ntibagomba kureka izo serivisi zifunguye kuri interineti yose kandi bakayungurura trafiki y'impimbano; abahohotewe bakoresha uburinzi bwa DDoS n'imbibi z'umuvuduko.",
     "Hila za DDoS ambapo mshambulizi hutuma maombi madogo yenye anwani bandia ya mwathirika kwa seva za umma zilizosanidiwa vibaya (NTP, DNS, Memcached) zinazojibu kwa majibu makubwa zaidi yanayoelekezwa kwa mwathirika.",
     "Mashambulizi ya Memcached ya 2018 yalifikia ukubwa wa rekodi hivyo. Waendeshaji hawapaswi kuacha huduma hizo wazi kwa intaneti nzima na wachuje trafiki bandia; waathirika hutumia ulinzi wa DDoS na kikomo cha kasi."),
    ("mimikatz", "Mimikatz", ["mimikatz", "lsass dumping", "credential dumping tool", "outil mimikatz", "zana ya mimikatz"], "attacks", "keys and Windows logo", {"fr": "Mimikatz", "sw": "Mimikatz", "rw": "Mimikatz"},
     "A well-known security tool, used by testers and also by criminals, that can read passwords, hashes and tickets from the memory of a Windows computer once an attacker already has high privileges.",
     "Defences: limit administrator rights, enable Credential Guard and LSA protection, keep systems patched, use unique local admin passwords and monitor with endpoint detection (EDR) that flags credential-theft behaviour.",
     "Un outil de sécurité très connu, utilisé par les testeurs mais aussi par les criminels, capable de lire mots de passe, empreintes et tickets dans la mémoire d'un ordinateur Windows lorsque l'attaquant a déjà des privilèges élevés.",
     "Défenses : limiter les droits d'administrateur, activer Credential Guard et la protection LSA, corriger les systèmes, utiliser des mots de passe administrateur locaux uniques et surveiller avec un EDR qui signale le vol d'identifiants.",
     "Igikoresho cy'umutekano kizwi cyane, gikoreshwa n'abagerageza ndetse n'abagizi ba nabi, gishobora gusoma amagambo y'ibanga, hashes na tickets mu kwibuka kwa mudasobwa ya Windows iyo umushimusi asanzwe afite uburenganzira bwo hejuru.",
     "Uburinzi: kugabanya uburenganzira bw'abayobozi, gufungura Credential Guard na LSA protection, kuvugurura sisitemu, gukoresha amagambo y'ibanga y'abayobozi bwa local yihariye no gukurikirana na EDR ibona kwiba amakuru yo kwinjira.",
     "Zana maarufu ya usalama, inayotumiwa na wajaribu na pia wahalifu, inayoweza kusoma nywila, hash na tiketi kutoka kumbukumbu ya kompyuta ya Windows pale mshambulizi tayari ana haki za juu.",
     "Ulinzi: punguza haki za msimamizi, washa Credential Guard na ulinzi wa LSA, sasisha mifumo, tumia nywila za kipekee za msimamizi wa ndani na fuatilia kwa EDR inayoashiria wizi wa vitambulisho."),
    ("cobalt-strike", "Cobalt Strike", ["cobalt strike", "cobaltstrike", "beacon payload", "c2 framework", "red team framework", "cadre c2", "mfumo wa c2"], "attacks", "red team console", {"fr": "Cobalt Strike", "sw": "Cobalt Strike", "rw": "Cobalt Strike"},
     "A commercial red-team tool for simulating attackers. Cracked copies are widely abused by ransomware gangs and state groups to control compromised computers through a 'beacon'.",
     "Defenders hunt for its traits: periodic network 'beaconing', unusual processes and known configuration patterns. Good defence is EDR, network monitoring, patching and blocking unusual outbound connections.",
     "Un outil commercial d'équipe rouge pour simuler des attaquants. Des copies piratées sont largement détournées par des groupes de rançongiciel et d'États pour contrôler des ordinateurs compromis via un « beacon ».",
     "Les défenseurs traquent ses traits : « beaconing » réseau périodique, processus inhabituels et motifs de configuration connus. Bonne défense : EDR, surveillance réseau, correctifs et blocage des connexions sortantes inhabituelles.",
     "Igikoresho cya red team cy'ubucuruzi cyo kwigana abashimusi. Kopi zacitswe zikoreshwa nabi cyane n'amatsinda ya ransomware n'ay'ibihugu mu kugenzura mudasobwa zagizweho ingaruka binyuze kuri «beacon».",
     "Abarinzi bashakisha ibimenyetso byayo: beaconing ya network ikorwa buri gihe, process zidasanzwe n'imiterere izwi. Uburinzi bwiza: EDR, gukurikirana network, patches no guhagarika imikoranire isohoka idasanzwe.",
     "Zana ya kibiashara ya red team ya kuiga washambuliaji. Nakala zilizovunjwa hutumiwa vibaya na magenge ya ransomware na makundi ya nchi kudhibiti kompyuta zilizoathirika kupitia «beacon».",
     "Watetezi hutafuta sifa zake: «beaconing» ya mtandao ya mara kwa mara, michakato isiyo ya kawaida na mifumo ya usanidi inayojulikana. Ulinzi mzuri: EDR, ufuatiliaji wa mtandao, viraka na kuzuia miunganisho isiyo ya kawaida inayotoka."),
    ("aircrack-wifi-auditing", "Wi-Fi auditing tools (Aircrack-ng)", ["aircrack-ng", "aircrack", "wifi auditing", "wi-fi auditing", "wifi cracking tools", "outils d'audit wi-fi", "zana za ukaguzi wa wi-fi"], "attacks", "wifi router and laptop", {"fr": "Outils d'audit Wi-Fi (Aircrack-ng)", "sw": "Zana za ukaguzi wa Wi-Fi (Aircrack-ng)", "rw": "Ibikoresho byo gusuzuma Wi-Fi (Aircrack-ng)"},
     "Aircrack-ng is an open-source toolkit that security testers use to check how well a Wi-Fi network resists password guessing and capture attacks. Criminals can misuse the same ideas against weak networks.",
     "To resist: use WPA3 (or WPA2 with AES) and a long random passphrase, turn off WPS, update router firmware and change the default admin password. Test only networks you own or have written permission to test.",
     "Aircrack-ng est une boîte à outils open source que les testeurs de sécurité utilisent pour vérifier la résistance d'un réseau Wi-Fi aux essais de mots de passe et aux captures. Les criminels peuvent détourner les mêmes idées contre des réseaux faibles.",
     "Pour résister : WPA3 (ou WPA2 avec AES) et une phrase secrète longue et aléatoire, désactiver le WPS, mettre à jour le micrologiciel du routeur et changer le mot de passe d'administration. Ne testez que des réseaux à vous ou avec autorisation écrite.",
     "Aircrack-ng ni ibikoresho bifunguye bikoreshwa n'abagerageza umutekano mu gusuzuma uko Wi-Fi irwanya kugerageza amagambo y'ibanga no gufata amakuru. Abagizi ba nabi bashobora gukoresha nabi ibyo bitekerezo ku miyoboro ifite intege nke.",
     "Kurwanya: koresha WPA3 (cyangwa WPA2 na AES) n'interuro y'ibanga ndende y'amahirwe, uzimye WPS, uvugurure firmware ya router uhindure ijambo ry'ibanga rya admin risanzwe. Gerageza gusa imiyoboro yawe cyangwa ufitiye uruhushya rwanditse.",
     "Aircrack-ng ni zana huria ambazo wajaribu wa usalama hutumia kukagua jinsi mtandao wa Wi-Fi unavyopinga kubahatisha nywila na kunasa. Wahalifu wanaweza kutumia vibaya mawazo hayo dhidi ya mitandao dhaifu.",
     "Kupinga: tumia WPA3 (au WPA2 na AES) na nenosiri refu nasibu, zima WPS, sasisha firmware ya router na ubadilishe nywila ya msimamizi chaguo-msingi. Jaribu mitandao yako tu au ile ulio na ruhusa ya maandishi."),
    ("exploit-broker-market", "Zero-day exploit market and brokers", ["exploit broker", "zero day market", "zero-day market", "vulnerability broker", "exploit market", "marché des zero-day", "marche des zero-day", "soko la zero-day"], "attacks", "marketplace stalls", {"fr": "Marché des zero-day et courtiers", "sw": "Soko la zero-day na madalali", "rw": "Isoko rya zero-day n'abahuza"},
     "A market where unknown software flaws (zero-days) and exploits are bought and sold by brokers, governments, companies and criminals. Some programmes pay researchers legally; others serve criminals or surveillance.",
     "It explains why patches matter and why bug bounty and coordinated disclosure are better paths for researchers. Users stay safer by installing updates quickly and by turning on automatic updates.",
     "Un marché où des failles logicielles inconnues (zero-days) et des exploits sont achetés et vendus par des courtiers, gouvernements, entreprises et criminels. Certains programmes paient légalement les chercheurs ; d'autres servent des criminels ou la surveillance.",
     "Cela explique l'importance des correctifs et pourquoi les primes aux bugs et la divulgation coordonnée sont de meilleures voies pour les chercheurs. Les utilisateurs sont plus protégés en installant vite les mises à jour et en activant les mises à jour automatiques.",
     "Isoko aho intege nke za porogaramu zitazwi (zero-days) na exploits zigurwa zigacuruzwa n'abahuza, za Leta, ibigo n'abagizi ba nabi. Izindi gahunda zishyura abashakashatsi mu buryo bwemewe; izindi zikorera abagizi ba nabi cyangwa gukurikirana abantu.",
     "Risobanura impamvu patches ari ingenzi n'impamvu bug bounty na coordinated disclosure ari inzira nziza ku bashakashatsi. Abakoresha barushaho kurindwa bashyiraho ivugurura vuba kandi bafunguye ivugurura ryikora.",
     "Soko ambapo udhaifu wa programu usiojulikana (zero-day) na exploits hununuliwa na kuuzwa na madalali, serikali, kampuni na wahalifu. Baadhi ya programu hulipa watafiti kihalali; nyingine hutumikia wahalifu au ufuatiliaji.",
     "Linaeleza kwa nini viraka ni muhimu na kwa nini bug bounty na ufichuzi ulioratibiwa ni njia bora kwa watafiti. Watumiaji hubaki salama kwa kusakinisha masasisho haraka na kuwasha masasisho ya kiotomatiki."),
    ("ransom-negotiation", "Ransom demands and negotiation", ["ransom negotiation", "ransom payment", "should i pay ransom", "paying ransomware", "negotiation de rançon", "negociation de rancon", "paiement de rançon", "mazungumzo ya fidia"], "operations", "negotiation table with warning sign", {"fr": "Rançon : demande et négociation", "sw": "Madai ya fidia na mazungumzo", "rw": "Gusaba incungu no kuyiganiraho"},
     "After a ransomware attack, criminals demand payment to unlock files or not to leak stolen data. Authorities generally advise against paying: it does not guarantee recovery and it funds more attacks.",
     "Best practice: isolate affected machines, keep evidence, restore from clean offline backups, report to the authorities and your bank or insurer, and get expert help before any contact. Some payments may also be illegal in some places.",
     "Après une attaque par rançongiciel, les criminels exigent un paiement pour débloquer les fichiers ou ne pas divulguer les données volées. Les autorités déconseillent en général de payer : rien ne garantit la récupération et cela finance d'autres attaques.",
     "Bonnes pratiques : isoler les machines touchées, conserver les preuves, restaurer depuis des sauvegardes propres hors ligne, signaler aux autorités et à votre banque ou assureur, et demander l'aide d'experts avant tout contact. Certains paiements peuvent aussi être illégaux selon le lieu.",
     "Nyuma y'igitero cya ransomware, abagizi ba nabi basaba kwishyura ngo bafungure dosiye cyangwa batamena amakuru yibwe. Ubuyobozi busanzwe buvuga kutishyura: nta ngwate yo kugarura kandi bitera inkunga ibindi bitero.",
     "Imikorere myiza: gutandukanya imashini zagizweho ingaruka, kubika ibimenyetso, kugarura muri backups zisukuye zidafite interineti, gutanga raporo ku buyobozi no kuri banki cyangwa ubwishingizi, no gushaka abahanga mbere yo kuvugana. Kwishyura bimwe bishobora no kuba binyuranyije n'amategeko ahantu hamwe.",
     "Baada ya shambulio la ransomware, wahalifu hudai malipo kufungua faili au kutovujisha data iliyoibwa. Mamlaka kwa ujumla hushauri kutolipa: hakuna hakikisho la kurejesha na hufadhili mashambulizi zaidi.",
     "Mazoea bora: tenga mashine zilizoathirika, hifadhi ushahidi, rejesha kutoka nakala rudufu safi nje ya mtandao, ripoti kwa mamlaka na benki au bima yako, na pata msaada wa wataalamu kabla ya mawasiliano yoyote. Baadhi ya malipo yanaweza pia kuwa haramu mahali fulani."),
    ("smart-contract-flash-loan", "Smart contract exploits and flash-loan attacks", ["smart contract exploit", "flash loan attack", "flash loan", "defi hack", "defi exploit", "reentrancy attack", "exploit de contrat intelligent", "shambulio la flash loan"], "attacks", "blockchain blocks and warning", {"fr": "Exploits de contrats intelligents et flash loans", "sw": "Mashambulizi ya smart contract na flash loan", "rw": "Ibitero kuri smart contracts na flash loans"},
     "Attacks on blockchain programs (smart contracts) that exploit bugs or price tricks, for example reentrancy flaws or flash loans, which borrow huge sums for a few seconds to manipulate prices inside one transaction.",
     "Because blockchain transactions cannot be reversed, funds stolen this way are rarely recovered. Projects need independent security audits and testing; users should avoid unaudited platforms and never invest money they cannot afford to lose.",
     "Attaques contre des programmes blockchain (contrats intelligents) qui exploitent des bugs ou manipulations de prix, par exemple des failles de réentrance ou des flash loans, qui empruntent d'énormes sommes quelques secondes pour manipuler les prix dans une seule transaction.",
     "Les transactions blockchain étant irréversibles, les fonds volés ainsi sont rarement récupérés. Les projets ont besoin d'audits de sécurité indépendants ; les utilisateurs évitent les plateformes non auditées et n'investissent jamais de l'argent qu'ils ne peuvent pas perdre.",
     "Ibitero kuri porogaramu za blockchain (smart contracts) bikoresha amakosa cyangwa amayeri y'ibiciro, urugero reentrancy cyangwa flash loans, zitira amafaranga menshi mu masegonda make zihindura ibiciro mu igikorwa kimwe.",
     "Kuko ibikorwa bya blockchain bidasubizwa inyuma, amafaranga yibwe atyo asubirana gake. Imishinga ikeneye isuzuma ry'umutekano ryigenga; abakoresha birinda imbuga zitasuzumwe kandi ntibashore amafaranga adashobora gutakara.",
     "Mashambulizi kwa programu za blockchain (smart contracts) zinazotumia hitilafu au hila za bei, mfano reentrancy au flash loans, zinazokopa kiasi kikubwa kwa sekunde chache kudanganya bei ndani ya muamala mmoja.",
     "Kwa kuwa miamala ya blockchain haiwezi kurudishwa, fedha zilizoibwa hivi hurejeshwa mara chache. Miradi inahitaji ukaguzi huru wa usalama; watumiaji waepuke majukwaa yasiyokaguliwa na wasiwekeze pesa wasizoweza kupoteza."),
    ("rug-pull", "Rug pull", ["rug pull", "rugpull", "exit scam crypto", "token rug pull", "arnaque rug pull", "ulaghai wa rug pull"], "social", "carpet being pulled", {"fr": "Rug pull", "sw": "Rug pull", "rw": "Rug pull"},
     "A crypto scam where creators hype a new token or NFT project, collect investors' money and then suddenly drain the funds and disappear, leaving the token worthless.",
     "Warning signs: guaranteed or huge returns, anonymous team, locked-out selling, pressure to buy fast and celebrity endorsements. Research the team and contract audits, and never invest more than you can afford to lose.",
     "Une arnaque crypto où les créateurs font la promotion d'un nouveau jeton ou projet NFT, collectent l'argent des investisseurs, puis vident soudainement les fonds et disparaissent, laissant un jeton sans valeur.",
     "Signes : rendements garantis ou énormes, équipe anonyme, vente impossible, pression pour acheter vite et soutiens de célébrités. Vérifiez l'équipe et les audits du contrat, et n'investissez jamais plus que ce que vous pouvez perdre.",
     "Uburiganya bwa crypto aho abakoze batangaza token cyangwa umushinga wa NFT mushya, bagakusanya amafaranga y'abashoramari, hanyuma bagatwara amafaranga bagahita babura, token ikaba nta gaciro igifite.",
     "Ibimenyetso: inyungu zemewe cyangwa nini cyane, itsinda ritazwi, kugurisha bidashoboka, gukandirwa kugura vuba n'abantu b'ibyamamare babishyigikira. Genzura itsinda n'isuzuma rya contract, kandi ntushore amafaranga arenze ayo ushobora gutakaza.",
     "Ulaghai wa crypto ambapo waundaji hutangaza tokeni au mradi mpya wa NFT, hukusanya pesa za wawekezaji kisha ghafla huondoa fedha na kutoweka, wakiacha tokeni isiyo na thamani.",
     "Dalili: faida ya uhakika au kubwa, timu isiyojulikana, kutoweza kuuza, shinikizo la kununua haraka na kuungwa mkono na watu mashuhuri. Chunguza timu na ukaguzi wa mkataba, na usiwekeze zaidi ya unachoweza kupoteza."),
    ("airtime-subscription-fraud", "Airtime and subscription fraud", ["airtime fraud", "subscription fraud", "sim registration fraud", "telecom fraud", "premium rate fraud", "fraude au crédit téléphonique", "fraude aux credits telephoniques", "ulaghai wa muda wa maongezi"], "attacks", "mobile phone and airtime", {"fr": "Fraude au crédit et aux abonnements", "sw": "Ulaghai wa muda wa maongezi na usajili", "rw": "Uburiganya mu mafaranga y'itumanaho n'ukwiyandikisha"},
     "Telecom fraud types: airtime fraud steals or resells call credit, and subscription fraud opens lines or accounts with stolen or fake identity to avoid paying or to run scams.",
     "Protect yourself by registering SIM cards only in your own name at official shops, never lending your ID, checking your lines on the operator's official service, and reporting unknown subscriptions or missing airtime to your operator.",
     "Types de fraude télécom : la fraude au crédit vole ou revend du crédit d'appel, la fraude à l'abonnement ouvre des lignes ou comptes avec une identité volée ou fausse pour ne pas payer ou mener des arnaques.",
     "Protégez-vous : n'enregistrez les cartes SIM qu'à votre nom dans des boutiques officielles, ne prêtez jamais votre pièce d'identité, vérifiez vos lignes via le service officiel de l'opérateur et signalez abonnements inconnus ou crédit manquant à votre opérateur.",
     "Ubwoko bw'uburiganya mu itumanaho: airtime fraud yiba cyangwa igurisha amafaranga y'itumanaho, subscription fraud ifungura imirongo cyangwa konti hakoreshejwe umwirondoro wibwe cyangwa w'impimbano kugira ngo batishyura cyangwa bakore uburiganya.",
     "Wirinde: andikisha SIM card ku izina ryawe gusa mu maduka yemewe, ntuzigere utiza indangamuntu yawe, genzura imirongo yawe kuri serivisi yemewe ya sosiyete, kandi ubimenyeshe iyo ubonye ibikorwa utazi cyangwa amafaranga abuze.",
     "Aina za ulaghai wa simu: ulaghai wa muda wa maongezi huiba au huuza upya salio, na ulaghai wa usajili hufungua laini au akaunti kwa utambulisho ulioibwa au bandia ili kuepuka kulipa au kufanya ulaghai.",
     "Jilinde: sajili laini kwa jina lako tu katika maduka rasmi, kamwe usikopeshe kitambulisho chako, kagua laini zako kwa huduma rasmi ya mtoa huduma na uripoti usajili usiojulikana au salio linalopotea kwa mtoa huduma wako."),
    ("prompt-leakage", "Prompt leakage and system-prompt extraction", ["prompt leakage", "system prompt leak", "prompt extraction", "system prompt extraction", "fuite de prompt", "kuvuja kwa prompt"], "attacks", "chatbot revealing hidden text", {"fr": "Fuite de prompt système", "sw": "Kuvuja kwa prompt ya mfumo", "rw": "Kuvuga kwa prompt ya sisitemu"},
     "Tricking an AI assistant into revealing its hidden instructions (system prompt) or private data it was told to keep secret, by clever or repeated questions.",
     "Never put passwords, keys or confidential rules in a prompt, assume it can leak, and keep secrets in server-side code. Add output filtering and monitoring, and limit what data the AI can reach.",
     "Tromper un assistant IA pour qu'il révèle ses instructions cachées (prompt système) ou des données privées qu'on lui a demandé de garder secrètes, par des questions astucieuses ou répétées.",
     "Ne mettez jamais mots de passe, clés ou règles confidentielles dans un prompt, supposez qu'il peut fuiter et gardez les secrets dans le code côté serveur. Ajoutez filtrage des sorties et surveillance, et limitez les données accessibles à l'IA.",
     "Kuyobya umufasha wa AI ngo agaragaze amabwiriza ye yihishe (system prompt) cyangwa amakuru bwite yasabwe kugumana, hakoreshejwe ibibazo by'amayeri cyangwa bisubiramo.",
     "Ntuzigere ushyira amagambo y'ibanga, imfunguzo cyangwa amategeko y'ibanga muri prompt, ukeke ko ishobora kuvuga, kandi ubike amabanga mu code ya seriveri. Ongeraho kuyungurura ibisohoka no gukurikirana, kandi ugabanye amakuru AI ishobora kugeraho.",
     "Kudanganya msaidizi wa AI kufichua maagizo yake yaliyofichwa (system prompt) au data binafsi aliyoambiwa aiweke siri, kwa maswali ya hila au ya kurudiwa.",
     "Kamwe usiweke nywila, funguo au sheria za siri kwenye prompt, chukulia inaweza kuvuja na uhifadhi siri kwenye msimbo wa upande wa seva. Ongeza uchujaji wa matokeo na ufuatiliaji, na punguza data ambayo AI inaweza kufikia."),
    ("rag-poisoning", "RAG poisoning", ["rag poisoning", "retrieval poisoning", "knowledge base poisoning", "document poisoning", "empoisonnement rag", "sumu ya rag"], "attacks", "documents with a poison label", {"fr": "Empoisonnement RAG", "sw": "Sumu ya RAG", "rw": "Kuroga RAG"},
     "Planting false or malicious text in the documents or web pages that an AI assistant retrieves (RAG, retrieval-augmented generation), so the AI repeats wrong facts or follows hidden instructions found in them.",
     "Defences: use trusted, access-controlled sources, treat retrieved text as untrusted data not as commands, log which sources were used, and have humans check important answers before acting on them.",
     "Planter du texte faux ou malveillant dans les documents ou pages web qu'un assistant IA récupère (RAG, génération augmentée par récupération), pour que l'IA répète de fausses informations ou suive des instructions cachées qu'il y trouve.",
     "Défenses : sources fiables et contrôlées, texte récupéré traité comme données non fiables et non comme commandes, journalisation des sources utilisées, et vérification humaine des réponses importantes avant d'agir.",
     "Gushyira inyandiko z'ibinyoma cyangwa mbi mu nyandiko cyangwa imbuga umufasha wa AI akura amakuru (RAG), bityo AI igasubiramo ibinyoma cyangwa igakurikiza amabwiriza ahishwe ayirimo.",
     "Uburinzi: koresha inkomoko zizewe kandi zigenzurwa, fata inyandiko zakuwe nk'amakuru atizewe aho kuba amategeko, andika inkomoko zakoreshejwe, kandi abantu bagenzure ibisubizo by'ingenzi mbere yo gukora.",
     "Kupanda maandishi ya uongo au hasidi katika nyaraka au kurasa za wavuti ambazo msaidizi wa AI hupata (RAG), ili AI irudie ukweli wa uongo au kufuata maagizo yaliyofichwa humo.",
     "Ulinzi: tumia vyanzo vinavyoaminika na vinavyodhibitiwa, chukulia maandishi yaliyopatikana kama data isiyoaminika si amri, rekodi vyanzo vilivyotumika, na wanadamu wakague majibu muhimu kabla ya kutenda."),
    ("ai-model-backdoor", "Backdoored AI models", ["backdoor attack ai", "ai backdoor", "model backdoor", "trojaned model", "poisoned model", "porte dérobée ia", "porte derobee ia", "mlango wa nyuma wa ai"], "attacks", "AI chip with a hidden door", {"fr": "Modèles d'IA à porte dérobée", "sw": "Mifano ya AI yenye mlango wa nyuma", "rw": "Moderi za AI zifite urugi rwihishe"},
     "An AI model that behaves normally except when it sees a secret trigger (a certain word, image pattern or sticker), then does what an attacker wants, because it was tampered with during training or in a shared download.",
     "Use models only from trusted sources, check hashes and signatures, prefer safe file formats, test models before use and keep a human in the loop for important decisions. Treat downloaded models like downloaded software.",
     "Un modèle d'IA qui se comporte normalement sauf face à un déclencheur secret (un mot, un motif d'image, un autocollant), puis fait ce que veut l'attaquant, car il a été altéré à l'entraînement ou dans un téléchargement partagé.",
     "N'utilisez des modèles que de sources fiables, vérifiez empreintes et signatures, préférez des formats de fichier sûrs, testez les modèles avant usage et gardez un humain dans la boucle pour les décisions importantes. Traitez un modèle téléchargé comme un logiciel téléchargé.",
     "Moderi ya AI ikora neza bisanzwe uretse iyo ibonye ikimenyetso cy'ibanga (ijambo, imiterere y'ishusho, sitikeri), hanyuma igakora icyo umushimusi ashaka, kuko yahinduwe mu gihe cyo kwiga cyangwa mu gukuramo gusangiwe.",
     "Koresha moderi ziva ahizewe gusa, genzura hashes n'ibimenyetso, hitamo imiterere ya dosiye itekanye, gerageza moderi mbere yo kuyikoresha kandi umuntu agume mu cyemezo cy'ingenzi. Fata moderi yakuwemo nka porogaramu yakuwemo.",
     "Mfano wa AI unaofanya kazi kawaida isipokuwa unapoona kichocheo cha siri (neno, muundo wa picha, kibandiko), kisha hufanya mshambulizi anachotaka, kwa sababu ulibadilishwa wakati wa mafunzo au katika upakuaji wa pamoja.",
     "Tumia mifano kutoka vyanzo vinavyoaminika tu, kagua hash na saini, pendelea miundo salama ya faili, jaribu mifano kabla ya matumizi na umweke binadamu katika maamuzi muhimu. Chukulia mfano uliopakuliwa kama programu iliyopakuliwa."),
    ("ai-supply-chain", "AI supply-chain risks", ["ai supply chain", "supply chain ai", "malicious model download", "pickle risk", "model hub risk", "chaîne d'approvisionnement ia", "chaine d'approvisionnement ia", "mnyororo wa ugavi wa ai"], "appsec", "package boxes and robot", {"fr": "Risques de la chaîne d'approvisionnement IA", "sw": "Hatari za mnyororo wa ugavi wa AI", "rw": "Ibyago mu rwego rw'ibigemurwa bya AI"},
     "Risks from the things an AI system depends on: downloaded models, datasets, libraries and plugins. A tampered model file or package can run malicious code or carry hidden behaviour.",
     "Pin versions, verify checksums and sources, scan dependencies, avoid loading unsafe serialized files (such as pickle) from strangers, and run unknown models in a sandbox with no access to secrets.",
     "Risques liés à ce dont dépend un système d'IA : modèles téléchargés, jeux de données, bibliothèques et extensions. Un fichier de modèle ou un paquet altéré peut exécuter du code malveillant ou porter un comportement caché.",
     "Fixez les versions, vérifiez sommes de contrôle et sources, analysez les dépendances, évitez de charger des fichiers sérialisés non sûrs (comme pickle) venant d'inconnus, et exécutez les modèles inconnus dans un bac à sable sans accès aux secrets.",
     "Ibyago biva ku bintu sisitemu ya AI yishingikiriza: moderi zakuweho, datasets, libraries na plugins. Dosiye ya moderi cyangwa package yahinduwe ishobora gukora code mbi cyangwa kugira imikorere ihishe.",
     "Shyiraho verisiyo zihamye, genzura checksums n'inkomoko, suzuma dependencies, wirinde gufungura dosiye zidatekanye (nka pickle) ziva ku batazwi, kandi ukoreshe moderi zitazwi muri sandbox idafite uburenganzira ku mabanga.",
     "Hatari zinazotokana na vitu ambavyo mfumo wa AI unategemea: mifano iliyopakuliwa, seti za data, maktaba na programu jalizi. Faili ya mfano au kifurushi kilichobadilishwa kinaweza kuendesha msimbo hasidi au kubeba tabia iliyofichwa.",
     "Funga matoleo, thibitisha checksums na vyanzo, changanua utegemezi, epuka kupakia faili zisizo salama za serialization (kama pickle) kutoka kwa wageni, na endesha mifano isiyojulikana kwenye sandbox isiyo na ufikiaji wa siri."),
    ("mcp-tool-poisoning", "AI agent and tool poisoning (MCP security)", ["mcp security", "tool poisoning", "agent security", "ai agent security", "mcp server risk", "excessive agency", "agent ia sécurité", "usalama wa wakala wa ai"], "appsec", "robot connected to tools", {"fr": "Sécurité des agents IA et empoisonnement d'outils (MCP)", "sw": "Usalama wa mawakala wa AI na sumu ya zana (MCP)", "rw": "Umutekano w'abakozi ba AI n'uburozi bw'ibikoresho (MCP)"},
     "AI agents can call tools (email, files, browsers, databases, MCP servers). Attackers can hide instructions in a tool description, web page or document so the agent leaks data or takes harmful actions.",
     "Give agents the least privilege, require human approval for sending, deleting or paying, use only trusted tools and servers, keep secrets out of reach, log every action and treat all fetched content as untrusted.",
     "Les agents IA peuvent appeler des outils (e-mail, fichiers, navigateurs, bases de données, serveurs MCP). Des attaquants peuvent cacher des instructions dans la description d'un outil, une page web ou un document pour que l'agent divulgue des données ou agisse mal.",
     "Donnez aux agents le moindre privilège, exigez l'approbation humaine pour envoyer, supprimer ou payer, n'utilisez que des outils et serveurs fiables, gardez les secrets hors de portée, journalisez chaque action et traitez tout contenu récupéré comme non fiable.",
     "Abakozi ba AI bashobora guhamagara ibikoresho (imeri, dosiye, browsers, databases, seriveri za MCP). Abagizi ba nabi bashobora guhisha amabwiriza mu gisobanuro cy'igikoresho, urupapuro rwa web cyangwa inyandiko kugira ngo umukozi asohore amakuru cyangwa akore ibyangiza.",
     "Haha abakozi uburenganzira buke, usabe ko umuntu yemeza kohereza, gusiba cyangwa kwishyura, koresha ibikoresho na seriveri byizewe gusa, ubike amabanga kure, wandike buri gikorwa kandi ufate ibyo bakuye byose nk'ibitizewe.",
     "Mawakala wa AI wanaweza kuita zana (barua pepe, faili, vivinjari, hifadhidata, seva za MCP). Washambuliaji wanaweza kuficha maagizo katika maelezo ya zana, ukurasa wa wavuti au hati ili wakala avujishe data au kufanya vitendo hatari.",
     "Wape mawakala haki ndogo kabisa, hitaji idhini ya binadamu kutuma, kufuta au kulipa, tumia zana na seva zinazoaminika tu, weka siri mbali, rekodi kila kitendo na uchukulie maudhui yote yaliyopatikana kama yasiyoaminika."),
    ("host-header-injection", "Host header injection", ["host header injection", "host header attack", "password reset poisoning", "injection d'en-tête host", "injection d'en-tete host", "host header"], "appsec", "web request header", {"fr": "Injection d'en-tête Host", "sw": "Host header injection", "rw": "Host header injection"},
     "A web flaw where an application trusts the Host header of an HTTP request, which an attacker can fake, to build links or emails, for example a password-reset link that points to the attacker's site.",
     "Developers should not trust the Host header: use a fixed list of allowed hostnames and configure the server and framework to reject others. Users should check where a reset link goes before entering data.",
     "Une faille web où l'application fait confiance à l'en-tête Host d'une requête HTTP, qu'un attaquant peut falsifier, pour construire des liens ou e-mails, par exemple un lien de réinitialisation de mot de passe pointant vers le site de l'attaquant.",
     "Les développeurs ne doivent pas faire confiance à l'en-tête Host : utilisez une liste fixe de noms d'hôte autorisés et configurez serveur et framework pour rejeter les autres. Les utilisateurs vérifient où mène un lien de réinitialisation avant de saisir des données.",
     "Ikosa rya web aho porogaramu yizera Host header y'icyifuzo cya HTTP, umushimusi ashobora guhimba, mu kubaka link cyangwa imeri, urugero link yo gusubiza ijambo ry'ibanga yerekeza ku rubuga rw'umushimusi.",
     "Abategura ntibagomba kwizera Host header: koresha urutonde ruhamye rw'amazina yemewe kandi ushyireho seriveri na framework bigahakana andi. Abakoresha bagenzure aho link yo gusubiza ijya mbere yo kwandika amakuru.",
     "Hitilafu ya wavuti ambapo programu huamini Host header ya ombi la HTTP, ambayo mshambulizi anaweza kughushi, kujenga viungo au barua pepe, mfano kiungo cha kuweka upya nywila kinachoelekea tovuti ya mshambulizi.",
     "Watengenezaji wasiamini Host header: tumia orodha maalum ya majina ya mwenyeji yanayoruhusiwa na usanidi seva na framework kukataa mengine. Watumiaji wakague kiungo cha kuweka upya kinakoenda kabla ya kuingiza data."),
    ("http-parameter-pollution", "HTTP parameter pollution", ["http parameter pollution", "hpp", "parameter pollution", "pollution de paramètres http", "pollution de parametres http", "uchafuzi wa vigezo vya http"], "appsec", "URL with repeated parameters", {"fr": "Pollution de paramètres HTTP", "sw": "Uchafuzi wa vigezo vya HTTP", "rw": "Guhumanya parameters za HTTP"},
     "Sending the same parameter several times in a request (for example amount=10&amount=1000) so that different parts of a system read different values, which can bypass checks or change behaviour.",
     "Developers should define clearly which value is used, validate input on the server and test how each layer (firewall, proxy, app) handles duplicates. Never rely only on client-side checks.",
     "Envoyer plusieurs fois le même paramètre dans une requête (par exemple montant=10&montant=1000) pour que différentes parties d'un système lisent des valeurs différentes, ce qui peut contourner des contrôles ou changer le comportement.",
     "Les développeurs doivent définir clairement quelle valeur est utilisée, valider les entrées côté serveur et tester la gestion des doublons à chaque couche (pare-feu, proxy, appli). Ne vous fiez jamais aux seuls contrôles côté client.",
     "Kohereza parameter imwe kenshi mu cyifuzo (urugero amount=10&amount=1000) kugira ngo ibice bitandukanye bya sisitemu bisome agaciro gatandukanye, bishobora kurenga igenzura cyangwa guhindura imikorere.",
     "Abategura bagomba kugena neza agaciro gakoreshwa, kugenzura ibyinjira kuri seriveri no gupima uko buri rwego (firewall, proxy, porogaramu) rukemura ibisubiramo. Ntukizere gusa ibigenzurwa mu ruhande rw'umukoresha.",
     "Kutuma kigezo kile kile mara kadhaa katika ombi (mfano kiasi=10&kiasi=1000) ili sehemu tofauti za mfumo zisome thamani tofauti, jambo linaloweza kupita ukaguzi au kubadilisha tabia.",
     "Watengenezaji wanapaswa kufafanua wazi thamani gani inatumika, kuhakiki ingizo kwenye seva na kujaribu jinsi kila tabaka (firewall, proxy, programu) linavyoshughulikia nakala. Kamwe usitegemee ukaguzi wa upande wa mteja pekee."),
    ("web-cache-deception", "Web cache deception and poisoning", ["web cache deception", "web cache poisoning", "cache deception", "empoisonnement du cache web", "tromperie de cache web", "sumu ya cache ya wavuti"], "appsec", "cache storage and web page", {"fr": "Tromperie et empoisonnement du cache web", "sw": "Udanganyifu na sumu ya cache ya wavuti", "rw": "Gushuka no kuroga cache ya web"},
     "Tricks that abuse web caches: in cache deception a victim's private page is stored as if it were public, and in cache poisoning a harmful response is stored and served to many users.",
     "Site owners should mark private pages as non-cacheable (Cache-Control: private/no-store), define cache keys carefully and test with their CDN. Users gain protection mainly from sites and CDNs that configure caching correctly.",
     "Astuces qui abusent des caches web : dans la tromperie de cache, la page privée d'une victime est stockée comme si elle était publique ; dans l'empoisonnement, une réponse nuisible est stockée et servie à de nombreux utilisateurs.",
     "Les propriétaires de sites doivent marquer les pages privées comme non cacheables (Cache-Control: private/no-store), définir soigneusement les clés de cache et tester avec leur CDN. Les utilisateurs sont protégés surtout par les sites et CDN bien configurés.",
     "Amayeri akoresha nabi cache za web: muri cache deception urupapuro rw'umuntu rubitswe nk'aho ari rusange, naho muri cache poisoning igisubizo kibi kibikwa kigatangwa ku bantu benshi.",
     "Banyiri imbuga bagomba kwerekana ko impapuro z'ibanga zidashobora gukorerwa cache (Cache-Control: private/no-store), bagena neza cache keys kandi bagapima na CDN yabo. Abakoresha barindwa cyane n'imbuga na CDN zishyizweho neza.",
     "Hila zinazotumia vibaya cache za wavuti: katika cache deception ukurasa wa kibinafsi wa mwathirika huhifadhiwa kana kwamba ni wa umma, na katika cache poisoning jibu hatari huhifadhiwa na kutolewa kwa watumiaji wengi.",
     "Wamiliki wa tovuti wanapaswa kuweka kurasa za faragha kama zisizoweza kuhifadhiwa kwenye cache (Cache-Control: private/no-store), kufafanua cache keys kwa makini na kujaribu na CDN yao. Watumiaji hulindwa zaidi na tovuti na CDN zilizosanidiwa vizuri."),
    ("cookie-attributes", "Cookie attributes (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)", ["httponly", "samesite", "secure flag", "session cookie", "cookie flags", "cookie attributes", "attributs de cookie", "attributs de cookies", "sifa za cookie"], "appsec", "cookie with shield", {"fr": "Attributs de cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)", "sw": "Sifa za cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)", "rw": "Imiterere ya cookie (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)"},
     "Settings that make cookies safer: HttpOnly stops scripts reading the cookie, Secure sends it only over HTTPS, and SameSite limits sending it with requests started from other sites. A session cookie identifies your logged-in session.",
     "Developers should set all three on login cookies to reduce session theft and CSRF. Users should log out on shared devices and keep browsers updated, because a stolen session cookie can give access without a password.",
     "Paramètres qui rendent les cookies plus sûrs : HttpOnly empêche les scripts de lire le cookie, Secure ne l'envoie qu'en HTTPS et SameSite limite son envoi avec des requêtes issues d'autres sites. Un cookie de session identifie votre session connectée.",
     "Les développeurs doivent activer les trois sur les cookies de connexion pour réduire le vol de session et le CSRF. Les utilisateurs se déconnectent sur les appareils partagés et mettent à jour leur navigateur, car un cookie de session volé peut donner accès sans mot de passe.",
     "Igenamiterere rituma cookies zirushaho gutekana: HttpOnly ibuza scripts kuzisoma, Secure izohereza kuri HTTPS gusa, SameSite igabanya kuzohereza n'ibyifuzo bitangijwe n'izindi mbuga. Session cookie igaragaza isomo ryawe ryinjiye.",
     "Abategura bagomba gushyiraho byose uko ari bitatu kuri cookies zo kwinjira kugira ngo bagabanye kwiba isomo na CSRF. Abakoresha bagomba gusohoka ku bikoresho bisangiwe no kuvugurura browser, kuko session cookie yibwe ishobora guha uburenganzira nta jambo ry'ibanga.",
     "Mipangilio inayofanya cookies kuwa salama zaidi: HttpOnly huzuia script kusoma cookie, Secure huituma kwa HTTPS tu, na SameSite hupunguza kuituma na maombi yaliyoanzishwa na tovuti nyingine. Cookie ya kikao hutambulisha kikao chako ulichoingia.",
     "Watengenezaji wanapaswa kuweka zote tatu kwenye cookies za kuingia ili kupunguza wizi wa kikao na CSRF. Watumiaji watoke kwenye vifaa vya pamoja na kusasisha kivinjari, kwa sababu cookie ya kikao iliyoibwa inaweza kutoa ufikiaji bila nywila."),
    ("csrf-token", "CSRF token", ["csrf token", "anti-csrf token", "anti csrf", "synchronizer token", "jeton csrf", "tokeni ya csrf"], "appsec", "form with a hidden token", {"fr": "Jeton CSRF", "sw": "Tokeni ya CSRF", "rw": "Token ya CSRF"},
     "A random secret value placed in a web form and checked by the server on submit. An attacker's page cannot know it, so forged requests sent from another site are rejected.",
     "Frameworks usually provide it automatically; developers must not disable it. Combine with SameSite cookies. As a user, log out of sensitive sites and avoid clicking unknown links while logged in.",
     "Une valeur secrète aléatoire placée dans un formulaire web et vérifiée par le serveur à l'envoi. La page d'un attaquant ne peut pas la connaître, donc les requêtes falsifiées venant d'un autre site sont rejetées.",
     "Les frameworks la fournissent généralement automatiquement ; les développeurs ne doivent pas la désactiver. Combinez avec des cookies SameSite. En tant qu'utilisateur, déconnectez-vous des sites sensibles et évitez de cliquer sur des liens inconnus en étant connecté.",
     "Agaciro k'ibanga k'amahirwe gashyirwa mu fomu ya web kakagenzurwa na seriveri iyo yoherejwe. Urupapuro rw'umushimusi ntirushobora kukamenya, bityo ibyifuzo by'impimbano biturutse ku rundi rubuga bihakanwa.",
     "Frameworks akenshi zirakazana ubwazo; abategura ntibagomba kukazimya. Rihuze na cookies za SameSite. Nk'umukoresha, sohoka ku mbuga z'ingenzi kandi wirinde gukanda link zitazwi wiyinjiriye.",
     "Thamani ya siri nasibu iliyowekwa kwenye fomu ya wavuti na kukaguliwa na seva inapotumwa. Ukurasa wa mshambulizi hauwezi kuijua, hivyo maombi bandia yanayotoka tovuti nyingine hukataliwa.",
     "Frameworks kwa kawaida huitoa kiotomatiki; watengenezaji wasiizime. Changanya na cookies za SameSite. Kama mtumiaji, toka kwenye tovuti nyeti na epuka kubofya viungo visivyojulikana ukiwa umeingia."),
    ("subresource-integrity", "Subresource Integrity (SRI)", ["subresource integrity", "sri", "integrity attribute", "sri hash", "intégrité des sous-ressources", "integrite des sous-ressources", "uadilifu wa rasilimali ndogo"], "appsec", "script tag with hash", {"fr": "Intégrité des sous-ressources (SRI)", "sw": "Uadilifu wa rasilimali ndogo (SRI)", "rw": "Ubutagomba bw'ibikoresho by'inyongera (SRI)"},
     "A browser feature where a web page lists the expected hash of a script or stylesheet loaded from another server (such as a CDN). If the file has been tampered with, the browser refuses to run it.",
     "It protects sites from a hacked third-party host (a supply-chain attack, like Magecart skimming). Add the integrity attribute to external scripts and keep the number of third-party scripts small.",
     "Une fonction du navigateur où une page web indique l'empreinte attendue d'un script ou d'une feuille de style chargé depuis un autre serveur (comme un CDN). Si le fichier a été altéré, le navigateur refuse de l'exécuter.",
     "Elle protège les sites contre un hébergeur tiers piraté (attaque de chaîne d'approvisionnement, comme le skimming Magecart). Ajoutez l'attribut integrity aux scripts externes et limitez le nombre de scripts tiers.",
     "Ikintu cya browser aho urupapuro rwa web rurondora hash itegerejwe y'agashya (script) cyangwa stylesheet ikuwe ku yindi seriveri (nka CDN). Niba dosiye yahinduwe, browser ihakana kuyikoresha.",
     "Irinda imbuga seriveri y'undi yahungabanyijwe (igitero mu rwego rw'ibigemurwa, nka Magecart skimming). Ongeraho integrity attribute ku ma script yo hanze kandi ugabanye umubare w'ama script y'abandi.",
     "Kipengele cha kivinjari ambapo ukurasa wa wavuti huorodhesha hash inayotarajiwa ya script au stylesheet iliyopakiwa kutoka seva nyingine (kama CDN). Faili ikibadilishwa, kivinjari hukataa kuiendesha.",
     "Hulinda tovuti dhidi ya mwenyeji wa mtu wa tatu aliyedukuliwa (shambulio la mnyororo wa ugavi, kama Magecart skimming). Ongeza sifa ya integrity kwenye script za nje na punguza idadi ya script za watu wengine."),
    ("iframe-sandbox", "Iframe security (frame busting, sandbox)", ["iframe", "iframe security", "frame busting", "sandbox attribute", "x-frame-options", "frame-ancestors", "sécurité des iframes", "securite des iframes", "usalama wa iframe"], "appsec", "page inside a page", {"fr": "Sécurité des iframes (sandbox)", "sw": "Usalama wa iframe (sandbox)", "rw": "Umutekano wa iframe (sandbox)"},
     "An iframe shows another page inside your page. Sites can forbid being framed (X-Frame-Options, frame-ancestors) to stop clickjacking, and can add the sandbox attribute to limit what an embedded page may do.",
     "Developers should block framing of sensitive pages and sandbox untrusted embeds. Old 'frame busting' scripts are unreliable; use headers instead. Users should not enter passwords on pages that look embedded inside another site.",
     "Une iframe affiche une autre page dans votre page. Les sites peuvent interdire d'être intégrés (X-Frame-Options, frame-ancestors) pour empêcher le clickjacking et ajouter l'attribut sandbox pour limiter ce que peut faire une page intégrée.",
     "Les développeurs doivent bloquer l'intégration des pages sensibles et mettre en sandbox les contenus non fiables. Les anciens scripts « frame busting » sont peu fiables ; utilisez des en-têtes. Les utilisateurs ne saisissent pas de mot de passe sur des pages qui semblent intégrées dans un autre site.",
     "Iframe yerekana urundi rupapuro mu rupapuro rwawe. Imbuga zishobora kubuza gushyirwa mu rundi (X-Frame-Options, frame-ancestors) kugira ngo zibuze clickjacking, no kongeraho sandbox attribute kugabanya ibyo urupapuro rushyizwemo rwemerewe.",
     "Abategura bagomba guhagarika gushyira impapuro z'ingenzi mu zindi no gushyira sandbox ku bitizewe. Ama script ya kera ya frame busting ntiyizewe; koresha headers. Abakoresha ntibandike amagambo y'ibanga ku mpapuro zisa nk'izashyizwe mu rundi rubuga.",
     "Iframe huonyesha ukurasa mwingine ndani ya ukurasa wako. Tovuti zinaweza kukataza kuwekwa kwenye fremu (X-Frame-Options, frame-ancestors) kuzuia clickjacking, na kuongeza sifa ya sandbox kupunguza kile ukurasa uliopachikwa unaweza kufanya.",
     "Watengenezaji wazuie kuweka kurasa nyeti kwenye fremu na kuweka sandbox kwa maudhui yasiyoaminika. Script za zamani za frame busting si za kutegemewa; tumia headers. Watumiaji wasiweke nywila kwenye kurasa zinazoonekana zimepachikwa ndani ya tovuti nyingine."),
    ("mime-sniffing", "MIME sniffing", ["mime sniffing", "content sniffing", "x-content-type-options", "nosniff", "sniffing de type mime", "kunusa aina ya mime"], "appsec", "file with wrong label", {"fr": "MIME sniffing", "sw": "MIME sniffing", "rw": "MIME sniffing"},
     "When a browser guesses a file's type from its content instead of trusting the declared type, an uploaded file that looks like an image might be treated as a script and run.",
     "Sites should send the header X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, set correct content types, store uploads outside the web root or on a separate domain and verify file contents. This blocks a class of upload and XSS tricks.",
     "Quand un navigateur devine le type d'un fichier d'après son contenu au lieu de croire le type déclaré, un fichier téléversé qui ressemble à une image peut être traité comme un script et exécuté.",
     "Les sites doivent envoyer l'en-tête X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, déclarer les bons types de contenu, stocker les téléversements hors de la racine web ou sur un domaine séparé et vérifier leur contenu. Cela bloque une catégorie de ruses d'upload et de XSS.",
     "Iyo browser ikeka ubwoko bwa dosiye ikurikije ibiyirimo aho kwizera ubwoko bwatangajwe, dosiye yashyizweho isa n'ishusho ishobora gufatwa nka script ikakoreshwa.",
     "Imbuga zigomba kohereza header X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, gushyiraho ubwoko bw'ibirimo neza, kubika dosiye zashyizweho hanze y'umuzi wa web cyangwa ku yindi domain no kugenzura ibiyirimo. Ibyo bibuza ubwoko bumwe bw'amayeri ya upload na XSS.",
     "Kivinjari kinapokisia aina ya faili kutoka maudhui yake badala ya kuamini aina iliyotangazwa, faili iliyopakiwa inayofanana na picha inaweza kuchukuliwa kama script na kuendeshwa.",
     "Tovuti zinapaswa kutuma kichwa X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, kuweka aina sahihi za maudhui, kuhifadhi mapakiwa nje ya mzizi wa wavuti au kwenye kikoa tofauti na kuhakiki maudhui. Hii huzuia aina moja ya hila za upakiaji na XSS."),
    ("graphql-websocket-security", "GraphQL and WebSocket security", ["graphql security", "websocket security", "graphql", "websockets", "graphql introspection", "sécurité graphql", "securite graphql", "usalama wa graphql"], "appsec", "API query and sockets", {"fr": "Sécurité de GraphQL et WebSocket", "sw": "Usalama wa GraphQL na WebSocket", "rw": "Umutekano wa GraphQL na WebSocket"},
     "GraphQL lets clients ask an API for exactly the data they want, and WebSockets keep a live two-way connection open. Both need the same care as other APIs, because attackers can send expensive or unauthorised requests.",
     "Defences: require authentication and per-field authorisation, limit query depth and cost, turn off introspection in production, validate the Origin of WebSocket connections and rate-limit messages.",
     "GraphQL permet aux clients de demander à une API exactement les données voulues, et les WebSocket gardent une connexion bidirectionnelle ouverte. Les deux exigent le même soin que les autres API, car des attaquants peuvent envoyer des requêtes coûteuses ou non autorisées.",
     "Défenses : exiger l'authentification et l'autorisation par champ, limiter la profondeur et le coût des requêtes, désactiver l'introspection en production, valider l'Origin des connexions WebSocket et limiter le débit des messages.",
     "GraphQL ituma abakiriya basaba API amakuru bashaka neza, naho WebSockets zigumana isano ifunguye y'impande zombi. Byombi bikeneye ubwitonzi nk'izindi API, kuko abashimusi bashobora kohereza ibyifuzo bihenze cyangwa bidafite uruhushya.",
     "Uburinzi: gusaba kwemeza no kugenzura uburenganzira kuri buri field, kugabanya ubujyakuzimu n'igiciro cya query, kuzimya introspection mu bikorwa, kugenzura Origin ya WebSocket no kugabanya umuvuduko w'ubutumwa.",
     "GraphQL huruhusu wateja kuomba API data hasa wanayotaka, na WebSockets hudumisha muunganisho wazi wa pande mbili. Zote zinahitaji uangalifu kama API nyingine, kwa sababu washambuliaji wanaweza kutuma maombi ghali au yasiyoruhusiwa.",
     "Ulinzi: hitaji uthibitishaji na idhini kwa kila uwanja, punguza kina na gharama ya query, zima introspection katika uzalishaji, hakiki Origin ya miunganisho ya WebSocket na punguza kasi ya ujumbe."),
]
